      "hints": [
        "Differentiate: $\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2(x+1) - (x+1)^{-2} = 0 \\implies 2(x+1)^3 = 1$.",
        "Second derivative: $\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 2 + 2(x+1)^{-3}$.",
        "Substitute $(x+1)^{-3} = 2 \\implies \\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 2 + 2(2) = 6$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Differentiate $y = (x + 1)^2 + (x + 1)^{-1}$ and set to zero for the stationary point $A$:\n$$\\frac{dy}{dx} = 2(x + 1) - (x + 1)^{-2} = 0$$\n$$2(x + 1) = \\frac{1}{(x + 1)^2} \\implies 2(x + 1)^3 = 1$$",
        "Find the second derivative of $y$ with respect to $x$:\n$$\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2} = 2 - (-2)(x + 1)^{-3} = 2 + 2(x + 1)^{-3}$$",
        "Substitute $(x + 1)^{-3} = 2$ from $2(x + 1)^3 = 1$ to evaluate $\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}$ at $A$:\n$$\\left.\\frac{d^2y}{dx^2}\\right|_A = 2 + 2(2) = 2 + 4 = 6$$"
      ]
    },
    {
      "part_id": "9709_s18_13_q11_ii",
      "difficulty": 4,
      "mapping": {
        "topic_id": "9709_p1_t_integration",
        "lesson_id": "9709_p1_t_integration_m05_l01"
      },
      "hints": [
        "Expand $y^2 = (x+1)^4 + 2(x+1) + (x+1)^{-2}$.",
        "Integrate: $[\\frac{(x+1)^5}{5} + (x+1)^2 - \\frac{1}{x+1}]_0^1$.",
        "Evaluate at $x = 1$ ($9.9$) and $x = 0$ ($0.2$) $\\implies V = 9.7\\pi \\approx 30.5$."
      ],
      "walkthrough": [
        "Expand $y^2 = \\left( (x + 1)^2 + (x + 1)^{-1} \\right)^2$:\n$$y^2 = (x + 1)^4 + 2(x + 1)^2(x + 1)^{-1} + (x + 1)^{-2} = (x + 1)^4 + 2(x + 1) + (x + 1)^{-2}$$",
        "Set up the volume of revolution integral from $x = 0$ to $x = 1$:\n$$V = \\pi \\int_0^1 \\left[ (x + 1)^4 + 2(x + 1) + (x + 1)^{-2} \\right]\\,dx$$",
        "Integrate using the reverse chain rule:\n$$V = \\pi \\left[ \\frac{(x + 1)^5}{5} + (x + 1)^2 - (x + 1)^{-1} \\right]_0^1$$",
        "Evaluate between the limits $x = 0$ and $x = 1$:\n$$\\text{At } x = 1: \\quad \\frac{2^5}{5} + 2^2 - \\frac{1}{2} = \\frac{32}{5} + 4 - \\frac{1}{2} = 6.4 + 4 - 0.5 = 9.9$$\n$$\\text{At } x = 0: \\quad \\frac{1^5}{5} + 1^2 - 1 = \\frac{1}{5} + 1 - 1 = 0.2$$\n$$V = \\pi(9.9 - 0.2) = 9.7\\pi \\quad (\\text{or } \\approx 30.5)$$"
      ]
    }
  ]
